WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.401 --> 00:00:03.977
Unit twenty-one. Accessible Web Design!

2
00:00:04.929 --> 00:00:09.598
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.648 --> 00:00:13.923
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.973 --> 00:00:18.307
Today we learn about Accessible Web Design. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:23.724
Accessibility. Say it with me. Accessibility!

6
00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:31.311
Alt text. Say it with me. Alt text!

7
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.776
Contrast. Say it with me. Contrast!

8
00:00:42.345 --> 00:00:46.396
Screen reader. Say it with me. Screen reader!

9
00:00:49.892 --> 00:00:53.386
Keyboard. Say it with me. Keyboard!

10
00:00:56.878 --> 00:01:00.442
Headings. Say it with me. Headings!

11
00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:07.800
Captions. Say it with me. Captions!

12
00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.013
Inclusive. Say it with me. Inclusive!

13
00:01:18.482 --> 00:01:31.654
Accessibility means everyone can use a website. Alt text describes images for a screen reader, good contrast helps reading, and headings organise content. Keyboard navigation and captions make sites inclusive.

14
00:01:31.704 --> 00:01:35.150
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:36.288 --> 00:01:41.502
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:41.552 --> 00:01:42.702
Contrast!

17
00:01:43.756 --> 00:01:49.180
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.380
Captions!

19
00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:57.258
Did you know? Many blind people use screen readers that read website text aloud!

20
00:01:57.308 --> 00:01:59.662
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:00.712 --> 00:02:08.137
Think and answer. Why is alt text important?

22
00:02:08.187 --> 00:02:09.366
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.483 --> 00:02:15.609
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:18.635
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

